1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Real-World Outdoor Stereo Transfer: From Benchmark to Volcanic Terrain.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Examining raw capture from Gunung stereo collection: 28.8 pixel median vertical misalignment.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Calibrated rectification using camera intrinsics reduces vertical residual to 2.4 pixels.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Cross-domain transfer: G1 Middlebury-optimized model reduces photometric warp error by 8.1 percent.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Physical region-of-interest diagnostics: sky saturation, building edges, grass foliage, and gravel.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Target adaptation: extended search range recovers near-field rocks; consistency filtering eliminates outliers.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Calibrated 3D metric reconstruction generates 127,000 valid points with physical depth from 0.6m to 35m.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Research conclusion: scientific rigor and geometric calibration are essential for real-world stereo transfer.
